## The verbs of UNDERGROUND V1, one action per handler of UNDERG.BAS. Line
## numbers in the comments are the 1979 program's. Taking, dropping, going
## and looking are the platform's own actions, bent to the original by the
## traits and clauses here and in the object files; every other verb is
## defined here, because the original gives each one a handler that tests the
## noun itself.

## Line 980: a room numbered above 14 is dark unless the sun lies in it, or
## the lamp is there (carried or not), lit, and has power left. Room 77 is
## dark whatever the lamp does.

define condition sun-lights: the minuature sun is here and not the player holds the minuature sun

define condition lamp-lights: the electric lamp is shining and the electric lamp is here and the player's lamp-life <= 300

define condition lit-up: sun-lights or lamp-lights

## Objects 0 to 32 can be carried and objects 0 to 15 are treasures (lines
## 3051 and 3052 draw both lines). The traits mark them for a reader. They
## cannot be tested: `the item is a treasure` compiles and is always false
## for a story trait, so the handlers below name the sixteen treasures.

define trait portable
  phrases en-US
    carried-about:
      It can be carried.
end trait

define trait treasure
  phrases en-US
    worth-points:
      It is worth 25 points in the building.
end trait

## GET, TAKE, CARRY and WEAR, lines 2085 to 2170. The count of line 2095
## refuses a tenth thing; it is kept on the player because nothing in Chord
## counts what a person holds. CORRECTED (O-12): line 2140, which makes the
## cat need its leash, cannot be reached in the original, because 2110 sends
## every ordinary thing to 2130 and 2130 jumps past it. The port reads 2110
## as `then2140`: a cat with no leash carried gets line 2150's refusal.

define action picking-up
  grammar
    get the item
    take the item
    carry the item
    wear the item
  refuse without item: what
  refuse when the player holds the item: not-here
  refuse when the item is scenery: dont-be-stupid
  refuse when the item is the rat and the rat is hungry: dont-be-stupid
  refuse when the item is the cat and the cat is aloof: dont-be-stupid
  refuse when the item is the cat and the cat is hungry: dont-be-stupid
  refuse when the player's burden > 8: too-many
  refuse when the item is the large emerald: emerald-falls
  refuse when the item is the minuature sun and not the player holds the space gloves: bare-hands
  refuse when the item is the uranium and not the player holds the space gloves: bare-hands
  refuse when the item is the minuature sun and not the player holds the radiation-proof container: nothing-to-carry
  refuse when the item is the uranium and not the player holds the radiation-proof container: nothing-to-carry
  refuse when the item is the cat and not the player holds the leash: nothing-to-carry
  raise the player's burden by 1
  lower the player's score by 25 when (the item is the something valuable or the item is the platinum wire or the item is the uranium or the item is the ancient statue or the item is the gold nuggets or the item is the gold record or the item is the gold garbage or the item is the gold pet's dish or the item is the silver or the item is the large diamonds or the item is the gold telescope or the item is the large emerald or the item is the rare coins or the item is the rare stamps or the item is the black pearl or the item is the golden key) and the player is in the Building
  raise the player's burden by 1 when the item is the glass bottle and the water is here and not the player holds the water
  move the water to the Adventurer when the item is the glass bottle and the water is here and not the player holds the water
  raise the player's burden by 1 when the item is the water and not the player holds the glass bottle
  move the glass bottle to the Adventurer when the item is the water and not the player holds the glass bottle
  move the item to the Adventurer
  phrase now-wearing when the item is the sunglasses
  phrase now-wearing when the item is the space gloves
  phrase done when the item is not the sunglasses and the item is not the space gloves

define action picking-up-nothing
  grammar
    get
    take
    carry
    wear
  refuse what

## INVEN, lines 1240 to 1246: one line per thing carried, in object order.

