## DRINK and EAT, lines 2280 to 2290.

define action swallowing
  grammar
    drink the item
    eat the item
  refuse without item: what
  the player must hold the item: not-carrying
  refuse when the item is the water: water-polluted
  refuse when the item is not the piece of cheese: dont-be-funny
  phrase cheese-poisoned
  change the story to dying

## OPEN and UNLOCK, lines 2300 to 2370. OPEN VAULT, as coded, puts the
## player in room 58.

define action opening-it
  grammar
    open the item
    unlock the item
    unloc the item
  refuse when the item is the safe: safe-needs-combination
  refuse when the item is not the vault: no-lock
  move the player to the Square Room

define action opening-nothing
  grammar
    open
    unlock
    unloc
  refuse when the player is in the Dwarf Door: door-is-open-stupid
  refuse when the player is in the Basement: locked-from-other-side
  the player must be in the North of Door: nothing-locked
  the player must hold the golden key: no-key
  phrase pushed-through-door
  move the player to the Basement

## KILL, HIT, FIGHT and ATTACK, lines 2380 to 2400.

define action killing
  grammar
    kill the target
    hit the target
    fight the target
    attack the target
    attac the target
  refuse without target: what
  refuse when the target is the cat: spca
  refuse when the target is the dog: spca
  refuse when the target is the dwarf: bare-hands-ineffective
  refuse when the target is the Gnome: bare-hands-ineffective
  refuse when the target is the robot: bare-hands-ineffective
  refuse when the target is the woman: invisible-force
  refuse are-you-crazy

define action killing-nothing
  grammar
    kill
    hit
    fight
    attack
    attac
  refuse what

