## FILL, lines 2550 to 2560. CORRECTED (O-8): line 2560 reads X%(19%)=-1%,
## which is past the end of X% and ends the 1979 program without a word. One
## letter off from O%(19%)=-1%, "the water is carried", and that is what the
## port does: at the lake or the bog the water is in hand, and "Done."

define action filling
  grammar
    fill
  refuse when the player is not in the Lake Shore and the player is not in the Edge of Bog: saliva
  raise the player's burden by 1 when not the player holds the water
  move the water to the Adventurer
  phrase done

define action filling-it
  grammar
    fill the item
  refuse when the item is not the glass bottle: are-you-crazy
  refuse when the player is not in the Lake Shore and the player is not in the Edge of Bog: saliva
  raise the player's burden by 1 when not the player holds the water
  move the water to the Adventurer
  phrase done

## READ, lines 2570 to 2640. CORRECTED (O-10): line 2610 tests object 19,
## the water, and prints a coin's legend. The port reads it as object 30,
## the penny.

define action reading-it
  grammar
    read the item
  refuse without item: what
  refuse when the item is the gold record: record-label
  refuse when the item is the glass bottle: bottle-label
  refuse when the item is the penny: penny-legend
  refuse when the item is the vault: suggest-look
  refuse when the item is the message: safe-message
  refuse nothing-written

## FEED, lines 2650 to 2750.

define action feeding
  grammar
    feed the animal
  refuse without animal: what
  refuse when the animal is not the rat and the animal is not the cat and the animal is not the woman and the animal is not the dwarf and the animal is not the dog: not-alive
  refuse when the animal is the woman: no-food
  refuse when the animal is the rat and not the player holds the piece of cheese: no-food
  refuse when the animal is the cat and not the player holds the rat: no-food
  refuse when the animal is the dwarf and not the player holds the lump of coal: no-food
  refuse when the animal is the dog and not the player holds the bone: no-food
  lower the player's burden by 1
  phrase rat-eats-cheese when the animal is the rat
  remove the piece of cheese when the animal is the rat
  change the cat to hungry when the animal is the rat and the cat is aloof
  change the rat to dead when the animal is the rat and the rat is hungry
  phrase cat-eats-rat when the animal is the cat
  remove the rat when the animal is the cat
  change the cat to fed when the animal is the cat and the cat is hungry
  phrase dwarf-eats-coal when the animal is the dwarf
  remove the lump of coal when the animal is the dwarf
  remove the dwarf when the animal is the dwarf
  phrase dog-takes-bone when the animal is the dog
  remove the bone when the animal is the dog
  remove the dog when the animal is the dog

## PUSH, PRESS and PULL, lines 2820 to 2840.

define action pressing
  grammar
    push the item
    press the item
    pull the item
  refuse without item: nothing-happens
  change the narrator to quiet
  change the narrator to speaking when the item is the remote-control box and the computer is humming and the narrator is quiet
  phrase ship-crushes when the player is in the Launching Area and the narrator is speaking
  phrase done when not the player is in the Launching Area and the narrator is speaking
  change the story to dying when the player is in the Launching Area and the narrator is speaking
  change the umpire to watching when the umpire is satisfied and the narrator is speaking
  change the umpire to satisfied when the Spaceship is at-port and the narrator is speaking
  change the Spaceship to on-planet when the Spaceship is at-port and the narrator is speaking
  change the Spaceship to at-port when the umpire is watching and the narrator is speaking
  change the narrator to spoken when the narrator is speaking
  change the narrator to speaking when the item is the cart and the player is in the Edge of Bog and the narrator is quiet
  phrase cart-rolls when the narrator is speaking
  move the ancient statue to the Edge of Bog when the narrator is speaking
  remove the cart when the narrator is speaking
  change the narrator to spoken when the narrator is speaking
  change the narrator to speaking when the item is the woman and the narrator is quiet
  phrase woman-irritated when the narrator is speaking
  change the narrator to spoken when the narrator is speaking
  change the narrator to speaking when the item is the lever and the narrator is quiet
  change the umpire to watching when the umpire is satisfied and the narrator is speaking
  change the umpire to satisfied when the Elevator is at-sphere and the narrator is speaking
  change the Elevator to at-junction when the Elevator is at-sphere and the narrator is speaking
  change the Elevator to between-floors when the umpire is watching and the narrator is speaking
  change the Elevator to at-sphere when the umpire is watching and the narrator is speaking
  phrase done when the narrator is speaking
  change the narrator to spoken when the narrator is speaking
  phrase nothing-happens when the narrator is quiet

## JUMP, LEAP, HOP and DIVE, lines 2850 to 2860. Off a height it kills.
## CORRECTED (O-9): anywhere else line 2860 is `goto2450`, the middle of the
## laser code, which prints a laser line and stops the program. 2540 with two
## digits swapped: "Nothing happens.", which is what the port says.

define action leaping
  grammar
    jump
    leap
    hop
    dive
  change the narrator to quiet
  change the narrator to spoken when the player is in the Observation Platform
  change the narrator to spoken when the player is in the Volcano View
  change the narrator to spoken when the player is in the Mountain Passage
  change the narrator to spoken when the player is in the North Side of Chasm
  change the narrator to spoken when the player is in the Chasm Bridge
  change the narrator to spoken when the player is in the Far Side of Chasm
  change the narrator to spoken when the player is in the Well
  change the narrator to spoken when the player is in the Gate
  phrase splat when the narrator is spoken
  change the story to dying when the narrator is spoken
  phrase nothing-happens when the narrator is quiet

## 2-7-3, lines 1290 to 1300.

define action dialling
  grammar
    two-seven-three
  refuse when the safe is sprung: hut-hut-hike
  the player must be in the Closet 80: hut-hut-hike
  phrase safe-slides-open
  change the safe to sprung
  move the Gnomes' silver to the Closet 80

## SCORE, lines 1270 to 1280.

define action tallying
  grammar
    score
  phrase score-line with points = the player's score with moves = the player's turns
  phrase class-f when the player's score < 100
  phrase class-e when the player's score >= 100 and the player's score < 200
  phrase class-d when the player's score >= 200 and the player's score < 300
  phrase class-c when the player's score >= 300 and the player's score < 400
  phrase class-b when the player's score >= 400 and the player's score < 500
  phrase class-a when the player's score >= 500

## The two fatal ways out, codes -6 and -8 of line 2870. They are actions
## and not `is deadly` exits because the platform's death ends the game, and
## the original's does not.

define action stepping-onto-the-planet while the player is in the Strange Planet
  grammar
    out
    exit
    leave
  phrase cyanide-atmosphere
  change the story to dying

define action stepping-into-the-volcano while the player is in the Square Room
  grammar
    south
    s
  phrase inside-volcano
  change the story to dying

## Three exits lead to a different room by state (lines 2820 and 2840 rewrite
## the map). A room has one exit per direction in Chord, so the second
## destination of each is an action that exists only in that room and state.

define action leaving-the-docked-ship while the player is in the Spaceship and the Spaceship is at-port
  grammar
    out
    exit
    leave
    door
  move the player to the Waiting Room

define action boarding-the-docked-ship while the player is in the Waiting Room and the Spaceship is at-port
  grammar
    west
    w
  move the player to the Spaceship

define action leaving-the-raised-elevator while the player is in the Elevator and the Elevator is at-sphere
  grammar
    south
    s
  move the player to the Sphere Room

## Lines 2020 to 2050: leaving a room by a way that exists, while its
## guardian is there, is fatal. Each is an action and not a clause on the
## room because a clause may not change anything and then refuse.

define action leaving-the-gnome while the player is in the Gate and the Gnome is here
  grammar
    north
    n
    south
    s
  phrase deadly-knife
  change the story to dying

define action leaving-the-dog while the player is in the Room 84 and the dog is here
  grammar
    west
    w
    northwest
    nw
  phrase dog-barks
  change the story to dying

define action leaving-the-robot while the player is in the Junction of Tunnels and the robot is here
  grammar
    north
    n
    east
    e
    west
    w
    south
    s
    northeast
    ne
    southwest
    sw
    up
    u
    climb
  phrase robot-fires
  change the story to dying

## Line 2010, the rat's bite. CORRECTED (O-11): the line tests
## `X%(11%)-30% AND O%(31%)-X%(0%)`, "the rat is not hungry and the rat is not
## here", which a hungry rat in the room never satisfies; the oracle lets you
## walk out. Read with `=` for each `-` it is the guardian the message
## describes: leave the room of a hungry rat and it bites.

define action leaving-the-rat while the player is in the North-South Room and the rat is here and the rat is hungry
  grammar
    north
    n
    northeast
    ne
  phrase rat-bites
  change the story to dying

## Line 2020: the dwarf lets you go any way but north.

define action passing-the-dwarf while the player is in the Dwarf City and the dwarf is here
  grammar
    north
    n
  phrase deadly-knife
  change the story to dying

## The four replies of lines 1940 to 1970.

define action cursing
  grammar
    fuck
  phrase headache

  phrases en-US
    headache:
      Not now-- I've got a headache.

define action crapping
  grammar
    shit
  phrase toilet

  phrases en-US
    toilet:
      Does this room look like a toilet?

define action helling
  grammar
    hell
  phrase get-there-yourself
  phrase what-about-it

  phrases en-US
    get-there-yourself:
      I can't help you there. You'll have to get there by yourself.

define action damning
  grammar
    damn
  phrase no-swearing
  phrase what-about-it

  phrases en-US
    no-swearing:
      Swearing is not allowed in this game. What the hell is wrong with you?

define phrases en-US
  nothing:
    {br}
  not-carrying:
    You aren't carrying it.
  woman-picks-up-laser:
    The woman picks up the laser, examines it, and causes it to disappear.
  woman-catches-laser:
    The woman catches the laser, examines it, and causes it to disappear.
  wall-materializes:
    The wall materializes back over the hole.
  sun-melts-ice:
    The sun melts the ice.
  cat-eats-rat:
    The cat eats the rat and appears ready for travel.
  dog-takes-bone:
    The dog takes the bone and leaves.
  dwarf-eats-coal:
    The dwarf eats your coal and leaves.
  cat-opens-vault:
    The cat pushes open the vault, then walks away in search of more food.{br}
    Inside the vault is a golden key!
  rat-eats-cheese:
    The rat eats the cheese and immediately dies.
  animal-sniffs:
    The animal sniffs at the cheese, and refuses it.
  rock-hits-gnome:
    The rock hits the Gnome on the head, and he falls down the cliff.
  woman-stunned:
    The rock hits the woman on the head, but she is only stunned.{br}
    She seems to be very angry at you. Your surroundings fade...
  dwarf-dodges:
    The dwarf dodges the rock quickly, and throws his weapon, killing you.
  rock-bounces:
    The rock bounces harmlessly off of the robot.
  water-polluted:
    The water in this game is polluted and unfit to drink.
  cheese-poisoned:
    The cheese tastes strange. Evidently it was poisoned, because you died  immediately after eating it.
  dont-be-funny:
    Don't be funny.
  safe-needs-combination:
    You cannot open the safe without a combination.
  no-lock:
    It doesn't have a lock.
  door-is-open-stupid:
    The door IS open, stupid!
  locked-from-other-side:
    The door is locked from the other side.
  nothing-locked:
    Nothing here is locked.
  no-key:
    You don't have a key.
  pushed-through-door:
    As you unlock the door, you are pushed through it. The door locks behind you.
  bare-hands-ineffective:
    Your bare hands are ineffective.
  invisible-force:
    An invisible force deflects your fists.
  no-gun:
    You don't have a gun.
  laser-empty:
    Your laser appears to be empty.
  specify-target:
    You must specify a target.
  chain-reaction:
    You are about to destroy an entire planet with a chain reaction.{br}
    You must be immediately removed from this game to prevent this...
  laser-alarm:
    A laser-sensitive alarm rings, and a blast from the ceiling{br}
    kills you.
  harmless-colors:
    The laser blast breaks up into a harmless display of colors.
  hole-blasted:
    A hole is blasted in the wall, wide enough for you to get through.
  computer-destroyed:
    The computer is destroyed.
  no-damage:
    The laser beam strikes it's target and does no damage.
  disintegrates:
    The laser beam strikes it's target and disintegrates it.
  emerald-sticks:
    The emerald sticks to your hand.
  mine-explodes:
    There is a loud explosion here, and you are blasted into millions of{br}
    pieces.
  explosion-below:
    There is a loud explosion below you.
  saliva:
    With what? Saliva?
  record-label:
    GNOME RECORDS, L. T. D.{br}
    EVERY TITLE A GUARANTEED GOLD RECORD{br}
    "GNOME ME" BY GERRY AND THE GNOMES{br}
    PRODUCED BY ARTHUR H. GNOME{br}
    MFG. BY GNOME RECORDS L. T. D.
  bottle-label:
    WATER:{br}
    NO DEPOSIT{br}
    NO RETURN
  penny-legend:
    In god we trust{br}
    Liberty{br}
    1979
  suggest-look:
    I suggest you LOOK to see what is written on it.
  safe-message:
    The safe of the Gnomes is near--{br}
    The combination is 2-7-36
  nothing-written:
    There is nothing written on it.
  not-alive:
    It isn't alive.
  no-food:
    There is nothing here you can use for food.
  ship-crushes:
    A spaceship lands on the launch area and crushes you.
  cart-rolls:
    The cart rolls into the bog.{br}
    An ancient statue flies out!
  woman-irritated:
    The woman is mildly irritated at your action. An invisible force pushes you into the wall.
  splat:
    A A A A a a a a a . . .                    <splat>
  hut-hut-hike:
    Hut-Hut-Hike!
  safe-slides-open:
    The Gnomes' safe slides open. There is silver inside!
  score-line:
    You have scored {verbatim:points} points out of 500 possible in {verbatim:moves} turns.
  class-f:
    This puts you in class F.
  class-e:
    This puts you in class E.
  class-d:
    This puts you in class D.
  class-c:
    This puts you in class C.
  class-b:
    This puts you in class B.
  class-a:
    This puts you in class A.
  game-is-yours:
    A cloud of smoke envelopes both you and the woman...

    You are somewhere overlooking the entire UNDERGROUND game.{br}
    There is a forest, with a building and a path leading through{br}
    the forest and into a cave. There is a lake in the middle of the{br}
    forest. Somehow you can see into the cave. There are three ancient{br}
    cities in the cave, two populated by short beings, the other abandoned.{br}
    A chasm separates two of the cities from the greater part of{br}
    cave. The cave also contains a room shaped like a barrel, above an{br}
    abandoned mine. To the north of the cave are a maze of passages and{br}
    an active volcano. To the south is a small swamp.

    Around you are various gold objects, plus countless other valuable{br}
    objects.

    A woman is standing before you. She says,{br}
    "The UNDERGROUND game is now yours. You now have all of it's{br}
    treasures, and all of it's secrets, inhabitants, and other objects.
  woman-wants-laser:
    A woman appears in a cloud of smoke and asks you for your laser.
  you-are-dead:
    You are dead.
  three-deaths:
    Sorry, but people who are incompetent enough to die three times in the{br}
    same game don't deserve the chance to make it four.
  rat-bites:
    As you walk away, the rat bites you and you die.
  deadly-knife:
    As you go, you are intercepted by a deadly knife.
  dog-barks:
    The dog barks wildly, and the City of Gnome awakens, all carrying{br}
    knives.
  ice-slippery:
    The ice is to slippery for you to move on.
  robot-fires:
    On your way out, the robot fires a laser blast which kills you.
  paralyzed:
    You are somehow paralyzed by the woman.
  blinded:
    Some light in the room you have entered momentarily blinds you.
  lamp-running-out:
    Your lamp is running out of power.
  lamp-out-of-power:
    Your lamp has run out of power.
  what-about-it:
    What about it?
  too-many:
    You can't carry so many things at once.
  bare-hands:
    You can't touch that with bare hands.
  nothing-to-carry:
    You have nothing in which to carry that.
  drop-contents-first:
    You must drop it's contents first.
  emerald-falls:
    The emerald falls out of your hand.
  emerald-stuck:
    The emerald is stuck to your hand.
  not-here:
    It isn't here.
  now-wearing:
    You are now wearing them.
  dont-be-stupid:
    Don't be stupid.
  done:
    Done.
  what:
    What?
  nothing-happens:
    Nothing happens.
  are-you-crazy:
    Are you crazy?
  spca:
    S.P.C.A. and humane society regulations clearly prohibit you from doing that.

## The platform's own words, replaced by the original's.

override message looking-room-dark
  I can't see a thing.
end override

override message going-too-dark
  I can't see a thing.
end override

override message going-no-exit-that-way
  You can't move in that direction.
end override

override message going-cant-go
  You can't move in that direction.
end override

override message going-no-exit
  You can't move in that direction.
end override

override message going-no-exits
  You can't move in that direction.
end override
